[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: DSL values are unchecked until something feeds them to the option surface

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-DSL-CHECKS-NOTHING-BY-ITSELF
TITLE: DSL values are unchecked until something feeds them to the option surface
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The DSL is sugar only, which means it asserts nothing: every constructor is a
plain attrset literal, and the sole thing that can reject a malformed value is
the normalized option surface it is checked against. Measured by evaluating the
DSL with its normalized argument bound to a throw -- every constructor still
worked, including the ones building values the surface rejects.

That is the intended design, and it has a consequence worth stating. The
barrel declares a dsl to normalized dependency edge that does not exist at
evaluation time, so a consumer that imports the DSL and hands the result
straight to the emitter passes through no type at all. The emitted file would
then be checked only by strictdoc, at export, where the two silent duplicate
cases are known not to fire.

The guarantee therefore lives entirely in the consumer's option declaration.
Either the emitter's entry point takes values already checked -- by declaring
its input with the normalized type rather than accepting a bare attrset -- or a
consumer can bypass the surface without noticing.

CONFIRMED by measurement in the repair step of the same milestone, which is why
this node is not filed a second time under another name. Rendering values.nix
and fixtures/foreign.nix through `emit.grammar` directly -- not through
lib/check.nix -- produces bytes IDENTICAL to both committed files, and with
check.elements gutted to the identity function the model-equal, foreign-roundtrip
and negative-fixtures checks all stayed GREEN. The emitter reads every key with
an `or` default, so it is blind to every weakening the types catch. lib/check.nix
now exists and checks/strictdoc-grammar-surface-live.nix gates it, but the bypass
itself is still reachable: nothing stops a consumer calling emit.grammar.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Noted while proving the DSL cannot weaken the types. It cannot, but "cannot
weaken" is a statement about a value that reaches the surface, and nothing in
the current wiring guarantees one does.
<<<
